Implement user story SKY-004-A: Express server routes, middleware, and error handling

## Story Description
Implement src/server.ts with Express app exporting named `app`, guarded listen(), and all route handlers: GET /health, GET / (static file serving from src/public/index.html via fs.readFileSync), GET /search, GET /cheapest. Include RAPIDAPI_KEY gating middleware and error handling for SkyscannerClient failures. Import FlightResult from SKY-002. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports named `app` (Express instance) separately from `listen()` so supertest can import without binding a port
- The `listen()` call is guarded by `if (import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href)` (ESM) or `if (require.main === module)` (CJS) matching the tsup output format so `vitest run` never binds a port
- GET /health returns 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- GET / returns 200 text/html with body equal to contents of src/public/index.html read at runtime via fs.readFileSync (not hardcoded inline); never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search with valid params returns 200 { flights: FlightResult[], count, searchedAt } where count === flights.length; adults defaults to 1 if absent; missing required param (from/to/date) returns 400 { error }; non-numeric adults returns 400 { error }
- GET /cheapest with valid params returns 200 with single cheapest FlightResult; adults defaults to 1 if absent; missing required param returns 400 { error }; empty SkyscannerClient result returns 404 { error }
- RAPIDAPI_KEY absent at startup → /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / unaffected
- SkyscannerClient throws error → 500 { error } without crash or unhandled rejection; searchedAt is ISO-8601 distinct per request; FlightResult imported from SKY-002 not redeclared inline





