8. Implement `GET /cheapest`: same param validation and 503 guard; call `SkyscannerClient`, if result array is empty return `404 { error }`, otherwise return `200` with the single cheapest `FlightResult`; catch client errors → 500 `{ error }`.
9. Guard the `listen()` invocation with the appropriate main-module check matching tsup output (`if (import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href)` for ESM, or `if (require.main === module)` for CJS) so importing `app` in tests never binds a port.
10. Verify by running `npx vitest run` (or the project test command) to confirm no port is bound and all acceptance criteria pass; if tests fail, adjust `server.ts` only.
